  "id": "implicit-causality",
  "term": "implicit causality",
  "definition": "Implicit causality is the tendency of some interpersonal verbs to suggest which person in a sentence is seen as the likely cause of an event. This verb-based bias can shape how people interpret later references such as pronouns, especially in causal sentence contexts.",
